@@ -0,0 +1,58 @@
+# TIFF spot-channel repair: PhotoCraft 0.15.1
+
+Based on upstream `28f3c18c0d11d69005d224a0a5d5edc56f1fe858` (workspace
+version 0.15.1). This replaces the previous 0.11/0.10 overlay; it is not a set
+of old source files copied onto the new release. In particular, current DICOM
+and IFF decode dispatch and import-only encode errors remain intact.
+
+## Supported export
+
+One spot channel in RGB or CMYK, with optional transparency, at 8-bit,
+16-bit integer and 32-bit float depths. RGB + transparency + spot has five
+samples; CMYK + transparency + spot has six. Without transparency these have
+four and five samples respectively. TIFF ExtraSamples is `[2, 0]` with straight
+transparency or `[0]` without it. The spot is an unspecified sample identified
+by Photoshop channel metadata, never a second transparency channel.
+
+CMYK TIFF uses separated photometric interpretation. Only its four color
+planes undergo the existing PSD/TIFF CMYK convention conversion. Its alpha
+and spot planes are independent. A single plain CMYK raster layer uses the
+existing native flat-image path, preserving its original C/M/Y/K separations
+instead of sending them through the RGB compositor. A new generic `encode_tiff_spot` entry point
+replaces the old patch-only RGB writer. Source DPI, profiles and layer data
+continue through the existing metadata/export paths.
+
+## Polarity and layers
+
+PhotoCraft's current document model uses coverage: zero = no ink, one = full
+ink. PSD/Photoshop spot planes use the reverse convention. The conversion
+occurs once on PSD import/export; TIFF reuses those exported spot bytes
+without a second inversion and restores coverage on import. The patched PSD
+behavior is preserved across all three supported depths. This does not change
+the painting engine's internal convention or brush behavior.
+
+The Photoshop layer-data repair omits an absent global mask instead of writing
+an empty `LMsk` record, and puts merged-transparency marker blocks before the
+layer block. Existing byte-order and layer channel compression code is reused.
+Newer upstream PSD/PSB and other file-format code is retained.
+
+TIFF import retains extra planes independently of the RGB/CMYK composite,
+restores spot name/color/solidity, and handles layered and flat TIFF. Invalid
+layer data can fall back to composite data while preserving the spot. Legacy
+Pascal names (1006) are used when Unicode names (1045) are absent, keeping
+transparency and DisplayInfo entries aligned. Both modern 1077 and legacy 1007
+display resources are recognized. Missing/truncated spot pixels are errors.
+
+## Verification
+
+Synthetic tests cover RGB and CMYK, opaque/transparent, flat/layered, three
+sample depths, four TIFF compression options, byte order, planar/chunky data,
+orientation, malformed spot buffers, truncated planes, damaged layers and legacy
+channel-name alignment. Supplied real Photoshop PSD/TIFF references are opt-in
+ignored tests, run explicitly with `PHOTOCRAFT_SPOT_PSD` / `PHOTOCRAFT_SPOT_TIFF`.
+Reference artwork is not committed or included in the replacement package.
+
+The build's validation report records executed commands and actual outcomes.
+Adobe Photoshop opening/painting and production RIP output must be checked
+on the user's machine; Rust round trips do not establish real-app acceptance.
+Credit for reporting and real Photoshop/printing testing: @jwinslett1.
